  },
  "expected_benefit": "Increase population diversity: higher std of performance and exploration objectives, higher distance_from_center and parameter_spread for some candidates, and a greater chance to discover higher absolute performance at the boundaries. Short-term trade-offs in mean performance are possible but should be offset by longer-term gains.",
  "validation_plan": "In the next iterations, check for (a) increases in std of performance and exploration objectives vs current stds (performance std 0.0018, distance std 0.0013), (b) some candidates with higher distance_from_center and parameter_spread than current means (distance mean 0.2221), and (c) improvement in best-candidate performance beyond current best 0.1072. The independent validator's improvement test will determine acceptance.",
  "confidence": 0.70
}
</decision>

The analyzer shows an exploration/exploitation imbalance driven by objective weighting: diversity objectives (distance_from_center weight=0.5, parameter_spread=0.25) are likely dominating guidance while absolute performance remains low (mean performance 0.1095, best 0.1141). A minimal, targeted change is to explicitly increase the performance weight so the optimizer favors measurable performance gains going into the next iterations.

